cible in: 4.0.stable, 4.1.stable, 4.2.stable, 4.3.stable, 4.4.1.stable, 4.5.beta\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.5.beta (80a219a58) - Fedora Linux 42 (KDE Plasma Desktop Edition) on X11 - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5090 (nvidia; 575.64.03) - AMD Ryzen 9 9950X3D 16-Core Processor (32 threads) - 62.33 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nDouble-clicking on LineEdit text doesn't select the word if it's only 1 character long. Normally, the entire word is selected no matter its length.\n\nTextEdit is not affected by this issue; it will select the word correctly, no matter its length. (However, behavior when selecting all the text by triple-clicking also differs: in LineEdit, the view of the text won't change, while in TextEdit, it'll scroll to the end of the text.)\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/5e46eda4-e834-4fbc-a392-bee271c26d47\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Double-click on text in LineEdit that is 1 character long (with whitespace before and after).\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[test_lineedit_double_click.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/21686277/test_lineedit_double_click.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/even